S3ATASK Version 1.3  READ.ME file
---------------------------------

Welcome to our Extended Task (ToDo) Manager V1.3

The archive should contain the following files:

\APP\S3ATASK3.APP                Main program

\APP\S3ATASK\S3ATASKH.OVL        Optional Help File Overlay
\APP\S3ATASK\S3ATASKP.OVL        Optional Print File Overlay
\OPD\S3APRINT.DYL                Optional Print File

README.NEW          'Get you started' instructions for new users (This file)
README.V12          Upgrade instructions for users of V1.2
	
HISTORY.TXT         Details of the various upgrades the program has gone through.

REGISTER.TXT        Details on how to register the program.
LICENCE.TXT         A legal licence

S3ATASK3.TXT        Instructions in ASCII Text format

This is a fairly complex program, so I would strongly encourage you to 
read the instructions and work through the tutorial.

However, if you still insist on flying blind:

     1.   Put S3ATASK3.APP in your \APP\ directory.

     2.   If you want to install the optional Help system, put the 
          S3ATASKH.OVL file into the \APP\S3ATASK\ subdirectory.

     3.   If you want to use the optional printing system, put the
          S3ATASKP.OVL file into the \APP\S3ATASK\ subdirectory, and
          the S3APRINT.DYL into an \OPD\ directory.  (Note that this
          library file will be common to all my programs, so you only
          need one copy on the system)

     4.   Install (PSION-I) and go for it !!

If you do get a problem, PLEASE read the full instructions first.  

All comments, and registrations, gratefully received.

If you wish to register, up-to-date details are in the file REGISTER.TXT

If you want to monitor progress on upgrades and enhancements, as well as see if 
any bugs have been reported, visit the home page on the World-Wide Web. The address is :  

	http://members.aol.com/alanrichey

Also, if you like the look of this program, why not have a look at my other 
programs.  A full list is as follows:

    S3ATASKx.ZIP    :  An Extended Task (ToDo) Manager.
    S3ADRAWx.ZIP    :  A Drawing/Icon Viewer/Editor.
    S3ACOLLx.ZIP    :  A Collection (Records, Books, Stamps etc) Manager.
    S3ABANKx.ZIP    :  A Personal Accounts package that includes all of the
                       following smaller programs as optional modules.
    S3AHOMEx.ZIP    :  A Home Inventory program based on the Quicken version.
    S3APLANx.ZIP    :  A Budget Planner based on the Quicken Financial Planner.
    S3AFUELx.ZIP    :  A Fuel Consumption Monitor.
    S3AINVx.ZIP     :  An Investment Tracking Program.
    S3AEXPx.ZIP     :  An Expense Account Monitor.

All of these programs also run on the S3C.

With the exception of S3ATASK, these programs are also available for the Siena, 
and just use the prefix 'SNA' rather than 'S3A, i.e. SNABANKx.ZIP
                                                                    
('x' denotes a version number)

